**StickZero**

A modular multi-tool firmware for M5StickC PLUS powered by ESP32.

**Project Status: Release v3.3**
Enhanced with Sensei AC support, Flashlight Mode, PC Audio Mute (BLE), Full TV-B-Gone (KIVI+All), Snake Game, and optimized power management.

---

**Features (v3.3)**
* **Bruce-Style Multi-Window GUI**: Categorized submenu navigation (`PC Remote`, `TV Remote`, `AC Remote`, `Flashlight`, `Snake Game`) with real-time battery percentage indicator (AXP192).
* **Language-Independent PC Control**: Hardware-level Windows 10/11 shutdown (`Win+X` -> `u` -> `u`), screen lock (`Win+L`), and audio mute (`KEY_MEDIA_MUTE`) via Bluetooth HID.
* **Full TV-B-Gone & KIVI Support**: Comprehensive IR power-toggle burst for KIVI, Samsung, LG, Sony, Panasonic, Philips, Toshiba, and TCL TVs.
* **Sensei & Universal AC Remote**: Dedicated payload generator for Sensei AC units alongside major climate brands (Gree, Coolix, Midea, Daikin, Haier, LG, Samsung, Panasonic, Mitsubishi).
* **Pocket Flashlight Mode**: Full-screen 100% white display brightness paired with on-board red LED (GPIO 10) illumination.
* **Retro Snake Game**: Interactive mini-game designed for the 240x135 LCD with score tracking.
* **Deep Power Saver**: Display backlight power rail (`LDO2`) completely shuts off after 10 seconds of inactivity to preserve battery life.

---

**Hardware Requirements**
* **Target Board**: M5StickC PLUS (ESP32-PICO-D4, ST7789 display 135x240 px).

---

**Project Structure**
* `include/display.h` / `src/display.cpp` — GUI rendering, menu state machine, flashlight, battery metering.
* `include/pc_controller.h` / `src/pc_controller.cpp` — Bluetooth HID shortcuts (Shutdown, Lock, Mute).
* `include/ir_controller.h` / `src/ir_controller.cpp` — TV (KIVI, Samsung, LG, Sony) and AC (Sensei, Universal) IR drivers.
* `include/game.h` / `src/game.cpp` — Built-in Snake game engine.
* `src/main.cpp` — Event loop & hardware orchestration.

---

**Build & Installation**
1. Open workspace in **VS Code** with **PlatformIO** extension.
2. Build & Upload:
   `pio run --target upload`

